WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:22.616
The Lion was the witch's slave, but he was not cooperating.

2
00:00:22.617 --> 00:00:32.883
"If I cannot ride you like a horse," called the Witch, "then I will starve you. Serve me or die—it is your choice."

3
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:37.070
The Lion roared loudly and leaped toward the Witch.

4
00:00:37.071 --> 00:00:49.528
"Maybe you'll change your mind," she said. "I will come back tomorrow."

5
00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:54.866
"Come into this yard, and I will bite you," said the Lion to the Witch.

6
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:59.658
The Lion wasn't worried about starving because he knew Dorothy would bring him food.

7
00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.628
Dorothy was the witch's slave too.

8
00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:07.256
And every night she sneaked out of her room and into the kitchen to steal food.

9
00:01:07.257 --> 00:01:12.651
She took the food to the Lion, and the two of them talked about their troubles.

10
00:01:12.652 --> 00:01:14.594
The Witch was unhappy.

11
00:01:14.595 --> 00:01:19.579
The Lion refused to serve her, and Dorothy still wore the silver shoes.

12
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.644
"I must get those silver shoes," said the Witch to herself.

13
00:01:24.645 --> 00:01:29.195
Dorothy never took the silver shoes off except when she took a bath.

14
00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:34.306
Luckily, the Wicked Witch was too afraid of the water to go into the bathroom.

15
00:01:34.307 --> 00:01:39.183
The Witch spent most of her time thinking of a way to steal the silver shoes.

16
00:01:39.184 --> 00:01:44.452
Finally she had a plan. She took an iron bar and made it invisible.

17
00:01:44.453 --> 00:01:52.151
Then she placed it in the middle of the kitchen, and she waited for Dorothy, who was busy working, to walk by.

18
00:01:52.152 --> 00:01:57.344
Dorothy had many things to clean, and she was carrying two big buckets of water.

19
00:01:57.345 --> 00:02:01.185
She couldn't see the invisible bar so she stumbled over it.

20
00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:05.353
She didn't fall, but one of her silver shoes came off.

21
00:02:05.354 --> 00:02:09.113
The Witch grabbed it and put it on.

22
00:02:09.114 --> 00:02:12.641
"Give me back my shoe!" shouted Dorothy.

23
00:02:12.642 --> 00:02:19.507
"I will not," replied the Witch. "It is my shoe now and not yours."

24
00:02:19.508 --> 00:02:24.652
Toto ran over and bit the Witch as hard as he could, but the Witch did not bleed.

25
00:02:24.653 --> 00:02:29.907
She was so wicked that her blood had dried up long ago.

26
00:02:29.908 --> 00:02:37.116
The Witch hit Toto hard with her broom. This made Dorothy angry.

27
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:39.856
"Evil Witch!" she screamed.

28
00:02:39.857 --> 00:02:44.584
In her anger Dorothy picked up a bucket of water and threw it at the Witch.

29
00:02:44.585 --> 00:02:48.901
The water soaked the Witch from head to foot.

30
00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:52.573
"No!" screamed the Witch.

31
00:02:52.574 --> 00:02:58.504
"Not water! Look what you have done! I am melting!"

32
00:02:58.505 --> 00:03:01.112
Dorothy could hardly believe her eyes.

33
00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:06.359
The Wicked Witch was melting, just as sugar melts in water.

34
00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.826
Dorothy was still afraid though.

35
00:03:08.827 --> 00:03:14.009
She took the other bucket of water and poured it on the bubbling heap.

36
00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:20.670
"My shoe," said Dorothy. She picked it up, dried it off, and put it back on.

37
00:03:20.671 --> 00:03:29.326
In the distance Dorothy could hear Toto barking.

38
00:03:29.327 --> 00:03:33.206
"Why is Toto barking?" asked the Lion.

39
00:03:33.207 --> 00:03:37.837
"He is happy," answered Dorothy, "because the Witch is dead."

40
00:03:37.838 --> 00:03:40.665
"Dead?" asked the Lion.

41
00:03:40.666 --> 00:03:45.358
"Yes, she melted when I threw the water at her," answered Dorothy.

42
00:03:45.359 --> 00:03:48.250
"I washed her wickedness away."

43
00:03:48.251 --> 00:03:52.616
The Lion was pleased, and he was happy to be free.

44
00:03:52.617 --> 00:03:55.875
Toto's barking brought the Winkies into the castle.

45
00:03:55.876 --> 00:04:01.788
"You are free!" shouted the Lion. "Just like me!"

46
00:04:01.789 --> 00:04:08.095
The Winkies immediately began to sing and dance for they had been slaves for many years.

47
00:04:08.096 --> 00:04:12.460
"I wish our friends were here to see this," said Dorothy sadly.

48
00:04:12.461 --> 00:04:15.952
"Let's try to save them," said the Lion.

49
00:04:15.953 --> 00:04:19.965
"Do you think we can?" asked Dorothy.

50
00:04:19.966 --> 00:04:24.780
"I didn't think we could kill the Wicked Witch," said the Lion.

51
00:04:24.781 --> 00:04:29.380
"But you did, so now I think anything is possible."

52
00:04:29.381 --> 00:04:33.169
"We will help you," said the oldest-looking Winkie.

53
00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.020
It took several days of searching.

54
00:04:36.021 --> 00:04:40.352
They found the Tin Man, but they found only the Scarecrow's straw.

55
00:04:40.353 --> 00:04:44.123
They brought what they found back to the Witch's tower.

56
00:04:44.124 --> 00:04:48.474
They repaired the Tin Man, and soon he was as good as new.

57
00:04:48.475 --> 00:04:52.681
"Thank you," he said. "But where is the Scarecrow?"

58
00:04:52.682 --> 00:04:58.917
"We could only find his straw," said Dorothy sadly. "His clothes are gone."

59
00:04:58.918 --> 00:05:02.347
"Oh yes, I remember," said the Tin Man.

60
00:05:02.348 --> 00:05:06.118
"The Winged Monkeys put the Scarecrow's clothes in a tree.

61
00:05:06.119 --> 00:05:19.330
Let us go there, and I will chop it down."

62
00:05:19.331 --> 00:05:24.773
At last everyone was reunited, and they made plans to return to Oz immediately.

63
00:05:24.774 --> 00:05:27.484
"I will get a heart," said the Tin Man.

64
00:05:27.485 --> 00:05:30.648
"I will get a brain," said the Scarecrow.

65
00:05:30.649 --> 00:05:34.228
"I will get some courage," said the Lion.

66
00:05:34.229 --> 00:05:42.930
"And I will go home!" said Dorothy happily.
